  "rationale": "This factor captures tail risk accumulation by combining absolute return magnitude with volume momentum. Absolute returns measure price disruption robustly, while the volume trend (short-term EMA / long-term EMA - 1) indicates whether volume is expanding during stress. A rising volume trend alongside large price changes signals informed pressure and may precede a continuation move. The 20-day sum reduces noise. This mutation improves on the parent by using absolute returns (more robust than squared) and a consistent volume trend indicator (EMA ratio) instead of a noisy volume-to-mean ratio.",
